--TEST--
a property, class constant or method written without `public`/`protected`/`private` is refused, and there is no implicit `public` to fall back on — `rule:core-api/written-visibility` and `rule:core-api/legacy-property-shapes-name-the-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Account {
    // `rule:core-api/legacy-property-shapes-name-the-visibility`: Novis's own grammar accepts this bare property shape, so
    // it is the omission the rule has to catch rather than a parse error.
    int $balance = 0;

    public function constructor(int $opening) {
        $this->balance = $opening;
    }
}
echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/declaring-a-class
--EXPECT--

